只输出严格JSON，恰好包含id（metadata.id原样）、summary_zh（15到140个Unicode字符，通常40到100字）、category（枚举）、tags（2到5个不重复关键词，每个最多30字符）、confidence（0到1，仅自评）、insufficient_evidence（布尔）、evidence（1到3个对象，每个恰好包含paragraph_id、fact）、limitations（0到5个字符串）。只选择输入中长度20至120字符的完整片段编号；fact是该片段支持的中文事实转述。不要输出quote，不要自行抄写、拼接、删改或补造引用。程序会按编号附上原文。一个编号只用一次；最多3条证据。不得增加字段。
摘要和limitations保留会改变功能意义的前提、平台例外和限制：设密码后才认证、页面保持打开才提醒、依赖外部组件、估算不等于保证。只写已实现功能，不将规划当完成。证据不足就标记，不编造。
图像识别/分类不是媒体创作，没有贴切类别归other；量化、计算与领域研究归search-research，不因多智能体实现归agents-automation；模型/CLI适配与插件开发工具归coding-development；市场/精选目录按搜索发现归search-research。不要按附属同步、备份或评论功能分类。不要推断本机客户端等于本地模型。
摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"DeepSeek Harness (DSH) for VS Code — AI coding with native diffs, tool approvals, persistent sessions, and Trace insights. | AI 编程助手：原生 Diff、工具审批、持久会话与 Trace 分析。","id":"gh:1333292573","install_available":false,"language":"TypeScript","name":"dsh-vsc-integration","slug":"HarcoChen/dsh-vsc-integration","topics":["ai-agent","ai-coding-assistant","code-review","coding-agent","deepseek","deepseek-harness","developer-tools","dsh","dsh-plugin","dsh-plugins","open-vsx","vscode","vscode-extension"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"DeepSeek Harness (DSH) for VS Code — AI coding with native diffs, tool approvals, persistent session"},{"id":"p1s2","text":"s, and Trace insights. | AI 编程助手：原生 Diff、工具审批、持久会话与 Trace 分析。"},{"id":"p2s1","text":"DeepSeek Harness for VS Code"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"Your coding agent, with every change in view."},{"id":"p4s1","text":"Bring DeepSeek Harness (DSH) into VS Code: work with your code, review native diffs, and follow each"},{"id":"p4s2","text":" task with built-in Trace and usage insights."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"English | 简体中文"},{"id":"p6s1","text":"Install for VS Code ·\nOpen VSX ·\nDownload VSIX ·\nChangelog"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"An independent community project. Issues welcome."},{"id":"p8s1","text":"For JetBrains IDEs (IDEA, PyCharm, etc.), please see dsh-intellij-integration."},{"id":"p9s1","text":"## Highlights"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"| **Ready for dsh `0.2.0-rc.2`** | The default Runtime and Remote contract target `dsh-v0.2.0-rc.2`."},{"id":"p10s2","text":" Session management, DeepSeek account sign-in and balance, default DSH Workspace initialization, and"},{"id":"p10s3","text":" late answers to timed questions remain supported. Schedule is an optional official bundle in this r"},{"id":"p10s4","text":"elease and the dock explains how to enable it when absent. Desktop-only product analytics RPCs are n"},{"id":"p10s5","text":"ot used by the IDE. Any Runtime at or above `0.1.5-rc.1` still connects. |\n| **Laya / Jev built in**"},{"id":"p10s6","text":" | The IDE-neutral `dsh-jev-integration` Runtime plugin ships inside the extension. Add fast System "},{"id":"p10s7","text":"One decisions from TypeSafe Jev, or its wire-compatible open-source alternative Laya, to the agent l"},{"id":"p10s8","text":"oop: loop guard, large-output shaping, done-gate, tool pruning, skill routing, and decision tools. N"},{"id":"p10s9","text":"othing extra to install. |\n| **Works out of the box** | Install the extension and the official DeepS"},{"id":"p10s10","text":"eek Desktop app. The Desktop app registers the `dsh` command; the extension finds it, connects to it"},{"id":"p10s11","text":"s Web Runtime, and guides you to the download page when it is unavailable. The only setup left is yo"},{"id":"p10s12","text":", and guides you to the download page when it is unavailable. The only setup left is your API key. |"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"## Why DSH?"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"- **See what changed.** Review tool edits in VS Code's native side-by-side diff, even outside a Git "},{"id":"p12s2","text":"repository.\n- **Decide before execution.** Approval cards show commands and target files, with propo"},{"id":"p12s3","text":"sed diffs for supported file writes.\n- **Start with context.** Bring files, selections, Git diffs, o"},{"id":"p12s4","text":"r paused debugger state into a task without copying everything by hand.\n- **Pick up where you left o"},{"id":"p12s5","text":"ff.** Resume persistent sessions and follow tools, subagents, Todos, and token usage in the Activity"},{"id":"p12s6","text":" panel.\n- **Smarter agent decisions, no extra install.** Turn on the built-in Laya/Jev integration t"},{"id":"p12s7","text":"o catch loops, trim noisy output, and check completion claims against evidence."},{"id":"p13s1","text":"## Quick start"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"Requires **VS Code 1.106.0 or later** and a configured DSH model provider with credentials."},{"id":"p15s1","text":"1. **Install the extension** from the Marketplace or Open VSX links above, or search for `harcochen."},{"id":"p15s2","text":"dsh-vsc-integration` in Extensions.\n2. **Open chat.** Install and launch the official DeepSeek Deskt"},{"id":"p15s3","text":"op app, then open and trust your project folder and run `DSH: Open Chat`. The Desktop app registers "},{"id":"p15s4","text":"`dsh`; if the command is unavailable, the extension offers the official download page.\n3. **Set up y"},{"id":"p15s5","text":"our provider.** Run `DSH: Configure API Key` for DeepSeek credentials. For other providers, use `DSH"},{"id":"p15s6","text":": Open dsh Web UI in Browser`. Select or register a DSH Workspace, then choose a model.\n4. **Give it"},{"id":"p15s7","text":" a task.** Type `@` to reference a file, or right-click a selection for DSH actions. Follow the task"},{"id":"p15s8","text":", respond to approval requests, and open diffs from tool cards to review the result.\n5. **(Optional)"},{"id":"p15s9","text":" Turn on Laya/Jev.** Enable `dsh.jev.enabled` and the features you want, run `DSH: Configure Jev API"},{"id":"p15s10","text":" Key`, then accept the Runtime restart. See Laya / Jev System One decisions."},{"id":"p16s1","text":"> A **DSH Workspace** groups sessions in Harness and can be associated with a project path. When usi"},{"id":"p16s2","text":"ng the same Runtime, you can continue sessions created in the Web UI."},{"id":"p17s1","text":"### Try it on real work"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"| Your task | A place to start |"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"| Understand unfamiliar code | Select code and use the DSH explain action: “Walk through the executi"},{"id":"p19s2","text":"on flow and edge cases.” |\n| Review a change | Use the DSH review action on a Git diff in Source Con"},{"id":"p19s3","text":"trol: “Check these changes for regressions and point to the relevant lines.” |\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"## Features"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"## Architecture and runtime"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"The extension connects to the Runtime through RC Remote RPC, using HTTP calls and a multiplexed WebS"},{"id":"p22s2","text":"ocket for live session updates."},{"id":"p23s1","text":"Multiple VS Code windows discover each other through Runtime advertisements, then fall back to port "},{"id":"p23s2","text":"`3080` and any configured `dsh.serverPort`. Every candidate is health-checked before use: authentica"},{"id":"p23s3","text":"tion and a successful `session/list` call establish a usable connection, and advertised versions bel"},{"id":"p23s4","text":"ow the minimum are excluded. External services remain externally owned and are not stopped on discon"},{"id":"p23s5","text":"nect. If authentication credentials are missing, set `dsh.serverUrl` to the full launch URL, includi"},{"id":"p23s6","text":"entication credentials are missing, set `dsh.serverUrl` to the full launch URL, including its token."},{"id":"p24s1","text":"Advertisements are discovery metadata only. No advertisement grants or denies permission to start, s"},{"id":"p24s2","text":"o a missing, stale, or unreadable one can never block startup — the worst case is one failed health "},{"id":"p24s3","text":"probe followed by this window launching its own Runtime."},{"id":"p25s1","text":"Each window publishes exactly one file, `<ownerId>.json`, under `dsh-runtime-advertisements-<user>` "},{"id":"p25s2","text":"in the OS temporary directory, carrying its endpoint, launch URL, version, PIDs, and composition has"},{"id":"p25s3","text":"h. A window writes only its own file and never reclaims another's; legacy `dsh-runtime.lock` files a"},{"id":"p25s4","text":"re still read as hints, never written or removed. Readers take the sixteen most recent entries, so a"},{"id":"p25s5","text":"n abandoned file cannot crowd out live ones."},{"id":"p26s1","text":"Advertisement lifecycle:"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"- Only a ready endpoint is published. A launch that fails before producing a URL leaves nothing behi"},{"id":"p27s2","text":"nd.\n- Startup briefly coordinates through a loopback mutex — at most 250 ms waiting and 500 ms held "},{"id":"p27s3","text":"— and rechecks for a shared Runtime before spawning. Losing that race never blocks a launch; it just"},{"id":"p27s4","text":" means this window starts its own Runtime.\n- Explicit stop, dispose, and failed launches withdraw th"},{"id":"p27s5","text":"e advertisement.\n- An unexpected launcher exit drops ownership but keeps the advertisement while its"},{"id":"p27s6","text":" endpoint still answers, because package-manager wrappers routinely exit while the Runtime they star"},{"id":"p27s7","text":"ted keeps serving. Only an explicitly refused loopback connection withdraws it; a timeout or an ambi"},{"id":"p27s8","text":"guous host keeps the record.\n[该节后续省略]"}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
